<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><meta name="description" content="1986 Faggin Aelle racer with original paint, Columbus steel, Shimano 600 and Cinelli handlebars."/><meta property="og:image" content="https://teob.dk/images/bikes/faggin-1986/hero.webp"/><title>Faggin Aelle 1986 · The Evolution of Bikes</title><link rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}/styles/global.css`}/></head><body><EnglishHeader current="bikes" danishPath="/cykler/faggin-1986/"/><main class="atala-page"><header class="quick-hero"><p class="section-label">In the collection · Padua, Italy · 1986</p><h1>Faggin<br/><em>Aelle</em></h1><p>An Italian steel frame in original net-pattern paint with Shimano 600, built as Japanese components became established on European racing bicycles.</p></header><figure class="quick-pass"><img src={`${images}/hero.webp`} alt="Red and white 1986 Faggin racing bicycle"/><figcaption>The Faggin from the drive side. Photo: The Evolution of Bikes.</figcaption></figure><section class="atala-facts"><div><strong>1986</strong><span>Stated year</span></div><div><strong>Columbus Aelle</strong><span>Lugged steel</span></div><div><strong>Shimano 600</strong><span>Groupset</span></div><div><strong>Cinelli</strong><span>Criterium bars</span></div></section><section class="atala-story"><div><p class="section-label">Faggin in Padua</p><h2>Frames built for the rider</h2></div><div><p>Former rider Marcello Faggin founded the company in 1945. Its Padua workshop became known for made-to-measure geometry, balance and finish.</p><p>This is not a team bicycle. Its lugs, chromed stays, small maker details and preserved paint instead show the workshop character in a road bicycle.</p></div></section><section class="atala-details"><figure><img src={`${images}/frame-finish.webp`} alt="Original Faggin net-pattern paint"/><figcaption>The mesh finish crosses the colour transition.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={`${images}/saddle-cluster.webp`} alt="Faggin seat cluster"/><figcaption>Slender stays and a small Faggin marking.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={`${images}/seat-tube.webp`} alt="Faggin name and coloured bands"/><figcaption>The frame carries a Columbus decal.</figcaption></figure></section><section class="atala-components"><div><p class="section-label">Shimano 600</p><h2>Italian frame, Japanese mechanics</h2></div><div><p>The controls, derailleurs, brakes and headset belong to Shimano 600, positioned below Dura-Ace. Campagnolo had long been expected on Italian quality frames, but by 1986 Shimano offered a genuine alternative.</p><p>Columbus Aelle was a dependable straight-gauge tubeset rather than the maker’s lightest competition series. The original paint and ordinary traces of use remain part of the documentation.</p></div></section><section class="koga-specs"><div><h2>Brief specification</h2></div><dl><div><dt>Maker</dt><dd>Faggin, Padua</dd></div><div><dt>Frame</dt><dd>Columbus Aelle steel</dd></div><div><dt>Gears and brakes</dt><dd>Shimano 600</dd></div><div><dt>Handlebars</dt><dd>Cinelli Criterium 65-42</dd></div></dl></section><section class="atala-closing"><p>The frame and paint came from Padua; Shimano supplied mechanics that kept pace with the decade.</p><div class="bike-bottom-nav"><a href={`${base}/en/bikes/`}>← Back to bicycles</a><a href={`${base}/en/periods/1980-1989/`}>View the period →</a></div></section></main><EnglishFooter/></body></html>
